 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? You' not alone in feeling that. Lots of people take a quick nap or go for a walk during the day. It' okay to take a short break every few hours. We're more productive in the end. Something active but easy, like a brisk walk or some light cardio. Avoid anything tense or heavy like lifting weights. Exactly. A quick walk is usually enough to clear your head and you' come back to your work with new energy. Let me know how it goes. And if the afternoon slump is real, a short nap is better than pushing through.",
